<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Deciding requests">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/rota/time-off">Time Off Requests</a> shows requests for the location. Filter with
            <strong>Waiting</strong>, <strong>Upcoming</strong> or <strong>All recent</strong>. Each request shows
            the person's remaining allowance, who else is off at the same time, and any warnings, such as
            shifts they're already on.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Approve</strong> or <strong>Reject</strong> a waiting request. The person is emailed either way.</li>
            <li>An approved request that hasn't finished can be withdrawn with <strong>Withdraw approval</strong>,
                or <strong>Cut short</strong> once it has started.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>You can't decide your own request. Another manager or an admin needs to.</HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Recording time off for someone">
        <FluentText>
            Use <strong>Record time off</strong>, for example when someone calls in sick. Choose the
            <strong>Staff member</strong>, <strong>Type</strong>, dates and hours. It's saved as approved
            straight away.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Types and allowances">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/rota/time-off/types">Time Off Types</a> lists the kinds of time off staff can choose,
            such as holiday or sickness. Each type has a <strong>Name</strong>, an optional description shown to
            staff, and whether it's <strong>Paid</strong> and <strong>Counts against an allowance</strong>.
            Archive types you no longer use. You can restore them later.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            Allowances are set per position, and can be changed for individuals on the Rota tab of their
            profile or in bulk on the <a href="/manage/rota/staff">Staff</a> page. The holiday year and the
            hours in a working day are in <a href="/manage/rota/settings">Rota Settings</a>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
